<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-LEADING TOUR OF THE MEDITERRANEAN PLACINGS. [CORRECTED 22:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>CYCLING-LEADING TOUR OF THE MEDITERRANEAN PLACINGS. [CORRECTED 22:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>VELAUX, France 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in</p>
<p>Thursday's two stages of the Tour of the Mediterranean cycle</p>
<p>race:</p>
<p>Second stage, Arles-Rognac (72 kms)</p>
<p>1. Mario Cipollini (Italy) Saeco  one hour 34 minutes 45</p>
<p>seconds</p>
<p>2. Fabio Baldato (Italy) MG Technogym</p>
<p>3. Henk Vogels (Australia) GAN</p>
<p>4. Massimo Strazzer (Italy) Roslotto</p>
<p>5. Johan Capiot (Belgium) TVM</p>
<p>6. Gordon Fraser (Canada) Mutuelle Seine et Marne</p>
<p>7. Endrio Leoni (Italy) AKI</p>
<p>8. Jann Kirsipuu (Estonia) Casino</p>
<p>9. Marco Zanotti (Italy) AKI</p>
<p> 10. Francois Simon (France) GAN   all same time as the winner</p>
<p>Third stage, team time-trial, Berrre-L'Etang-Velaux (19kms)</p>
<p> 1. Festina			 21 minutes 51.85 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Batik					   5.25 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Saeco					  23.76 secs</p>
<p> 4. Polti					  26.57</p>
<p> 5. Roslotto				     30.63</p>
<p> 6. GAN					    30.86</p>
<p> 7. Casino					 42.00</p>
<p> 8. AKI					    45.02</p>
<p> 9. Rabobank				     46.94</p>
<p> 10. Telekom				     49.96</p>
<p>Leading overall placings:</p>
<p>1. Emmanuel Magnien (France) Festina  4 hours 02 minutes five</p>
<p>seconds (corrects Magnien's time)</p>
<p>2. Richard Virenque (France) Festina</p>
<p>3. Didier Rous (France) Festina</p>
<p>4. Christophe Moreau (France) Festina</p>
<p>5. Laurent Dufaux (Switzerland) Festina  all same time as the</p>
<p>leader</p>
<p> 6. Francesco Frattini (Italy) Batik	 4.25 secs behind</p>
<p>7. Jon Odriozola (Spain) Batik</p>
<p>8. Luca Colombo (Italy) Batik</p>
<p>9. Simone Bertoletti (Italy) Batik</p>
<p> 10. Gabriele Colombo (Italy) Batik   all same time as Frattini</p>
